# No Cursor commit attribution

Never add any of the following to commit messages, PR bodies, or code comments:

- `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`
- `Co-authored-by: Cursor`
- `Made-with: Cursor`
- Any other Cursor / cursoragent attribution trailer or footer

When creating or amending commits:

1. Write only the human author message (subject + body).
2. Do not pass `--trailer` flags that attribute the change to Cursor.
3. After amend/commit, if a Cursor trailer appears, strip it immediately and force-with-lease only on the current non-main feature branch when the user asked to remove it.

Prefer project/local authorship only (`Thieu Nguyen` / the repo's configured user).
